  "question": {
    "text": "One mole of an ideal gas as taken from state&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> to state&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> by three different processes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>ACB</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>ADB</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>AEB</mi></math> as shown in the<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>V</mi></math> diagram. The heat absorbed by the gas is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0013_ac30896ad021.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 199px; height: 152px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Greater in process (b) than in (a)",
